# Corner benchmark: 15x15 with wild NE/SW corners, demonstrating numbered
# scan-order regions (digit tiers). Seeded RECORDBREAKER across the 13-long
# 21-Across with a crossing H. Region tiers: NW block = 0 (branched first),
# central hub = 1, everything else plain '.' (untiered, branched last).
#
#   orca fill grids/bench_corner.grid <spreadthewordlist.dict> -n 0 \
#       --disallow-shared-substring 6
#
# -> 16 solutions in ~34,981 nodes (~15s). The same grid with the digit tiers
#    replaced by plain '.' takes ~150,403 nodes (~86s) -- the numbered regions
#    give ~5.7x here (exact figures depend on the wordlist). Needs a full
#    Spread-the-Wordlist dictionary (bring your own; not bundled in this repo).
15 15
000000#####****
0000000###*****
00000000#******
00000000#******
#00000H0#******
##RECORDBREAKER
#####11111....#
##...11111...##
#....11111#####
.....11111...##
******#.......#
******#........
******#........
*****###.......
****#####......
